    "slides": [
      {
        "index": 1,
        "text": "Sitting with a spreadsheet at thirty-five, watching numbers that refuse to balance, a memory from twenty years ago suddenly settles into place.",
        "closing": false,
        "text_tone": "DARK",
        "logo_tone": "DARK",
        "footer_tone": "PLUM",
        "accent": "PLUM"
      },
      {
        "index": 2,
        "text": "You remember your father standing by the window on a Tuesday afternoon, staring into the yard for hours without speaking.",
        "closing": false,
        "text_tone": "DARK",
        "logo_tone": "DARK",
        "footer_tone": "PLUM",
        "accent": "PLUM"
      },
      {
        "index": 3,
        "text": "At ten, that silence felt cold and immense, like a door pulled shut against the rest of the house.",
        "closing": false,
        "text_tone": "DARK",
        "logo_tone": "DARK",
        "footer_tone": "PLUM",
        "accent": "PLUM"
      },
      {
        "index": 4,
        "text": "At thirty-five, holding your quiet panic, you recognize someone trying hard not to let their hands shake before their kids.",
        "closing": false,
        "text_tone": "DARK",
        "logo_tone": "DARK",
        "footer_tone": "PLUM",
        "accent": "PLUM"
      },
      {
        "index": 5,
        "text": "Silence in a home does not always mean emotional distance. Sometimes it is the heavy, invisible labor of keeping fear outside the threshold.",
        "closing": true,
        "text_tone": "DARK",
        "logo_tone": "DARK",
        "footer_tone": "PLUM",
        "accent": "PLUM"
      }
    ]
